Oz: the cgame predicts the server's auto hop. A server running pmove_AutoHop (game patch 0008; on by
default under id's rules too, Ozmium 2026-11-01) jumps again as a held jump lands; Oz's cgame never set
bg_autoHop, so it predicted no hop where the server hopped, and every held jump was a prediction miss at
its landing. It reads pmove_AutoHop from the server's systeminfo string: a server without it (id's game)
doesn't hop, and neither does the prediction. Not a cvar of the cgame's: on a listen server the cgame's
registration, with its own default, reset the server's, and no one hopped.

diff --git a/code/cgame/cg_predict.c b/code/cgame/cg_predict.c
--- a/code/cgame/cg_predict.c
+++ b/code/cgame/cg_predict.c
@@ -547,6 +547,10 @@ void CG_PredictPlayerState( void ) {
 		cg_pmove.tracemask &= ~CONTENTS_BODY;	// spectators can fly through bodies
 	}
 	cg_pmove.noFootsteps = ( cgs.dmflags & DF_NO_FOOTSTEPS ) > 0;
+	// Oz: hop as the server does (g_active.c G_AutoHop puts pmove_AutoHop in its systeminfo; id's game hasn't
+	// one and doesn't hop), or every held jump mispredicts. Read from the configstring, not a cvar of the
+	// cgame's: on a listen server that registration reset the server's own
+	bg_autoHop = atoi( Info_ValueForKey( CG_ConfigString( CS_SYSTEMINFO ), "pmove_AutoHop" ) );
 
 	// save the state before the pmove so we can detect transitions
 	oldPlayerState = cg.predictedPlayerState;
